# Greene et al. (2024), ApJ 964, 39 (arXiv:2309.05714v1), Table 4 (published numbering; identical in arXiv v1): UV LF of UNCOVER red broad-line AGN
# Redshift: 6.5 < z < 8.5 ("z~7-8 sample")
# Magnitude definition: M_UV measured at rest-frame 1450 A (Fig. 7 caption) -> M1450; lensing-corrected
# Phi convention: linear Phi in units of 1e-5 cMpc^-3 mag^-1 (H0=70), symmetric 1-sigma errors
# Note: checked against the primary paper (same values as the Grazian et al. 2024 Table 1 compilation).
# Note: the table note says 0.5-mag bins, but this sample is listed at 1-mag spacing (-19, -18, -17); 1, 2 and 2 objects.
# Note: the UV is a small, reddened fraction of the AGN light; not a classical unobscured-quasar UV LF.
#
# M1450  Phi  Delta
-19.0  1.3  0.5
-18.0  2.6  0.7
-17.0  4.0  1.0
